{
  "id": "calcium_chloride_water_solutions",
  "title": "Calcium Chloride Water Solutions",
  "description": "Freezing point, density, specific heat and dynamic viscosity of Calcium Chloride Water coolants",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "# Calcium Chloride Water Solutions\n\nCalculate and explore freezing point, density, specific heat, and dynamic viscosity of calcium chloride water solutions based on concentration."
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "concentration",
          "label": "Calcium Chloride Concentration",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": 10,
              "label": "10% by mass"
            },
            {
              "value": 20,
              "label": "20% by mass"
            },
            {
              "value": 30,
              "label": "30% by mass"
            },
            {
              "value": 40,
              "label": "40% by mass"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": 20
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "specific_gravity",
          "label": "Specific Gravity (at 60°F, 15.6°C)",
          "formula": "inputs.concentration == 10 ? 1.090 : inputs.concentration == 20 ? 1.189 : inputs.concentration == 30 ? 1.298 : 1.416",
          "unit": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "freezing_point_f",
          "label": "Freezing Point",
          "formula": "inputs.concentration == 10 ? 20 : inputs.concentration == 20 ? -4 : inputs.concentration == 30 ? -52 : 61",
          "unit": "°F"
        },
        {
          "id": "freezing_point_c",
          "label": "Freezing Point",
          "formula": "inputs.concentration == 10 ? -6.7 : inputs.concentration == 20 ? -20 : inputs.concentration == 30 ? -47 : 16",
          "unit": "°C"
        },
        {
          "id": "boiling_point_f",
          "label": "Boiling Point",
          "formula": "inputs.concentration == 10 ? 215 : inputs.concentration == 20 ? 220 : inputs.concentration == 30 ? 231 : 247",
          "unit": "°F"
        },
        {
          "id": "boiling_point_c",
          "label": "Boiling Point",
          "formula": "inputs.concentration == 10 ? 102 : inputs.concentration == 20 ? 104 : inputs.concentration == 30 ? 111 : 119",
          "unit": "°C"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Concentration (% by mass)",
        "Specific Gravity (60°F)",
        "Freezing Point (°F)",
        "Freezing Point (°C)",
        "Boiling Point (°F)",
        "Boiling Point (°C)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          10,
          1.09,
          20,
          -6.7,
          215,
          102
        ],
        [
          20,
          1.189,
          -4,
          -20,
          220,
          104
        ],
        [
          30,
          1.298,
          -52,
          -47,
          231,
          111
        ],
        [
          40,
          1.416,
          61,
          16,
          247,
          119
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Important Notes\n\n- **Eutectic Point**: The eutectic point occurs at approximately 29.92% calcium chloride concentration, which represents the lowest freezing point for calcium chloride water solutions.\n- **Specific Gravity**: Measured at 60°F (15.6°C)\n- **Applications**: Calcium chloride water solutions are commonly used as coolants and de-icing agents\n- **Density**: Increases with calcium chloride concentration\n- **Viscosity**: Dynamic viscosity varies with both concentration and temperature"
    }
  ]
}